<section class="hero process-hero"><div class="shell reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Every Project. One System. Zero Guesswork.</p><h1>The 14-stage project lifecycle</h1><p>Mid City Home Restoration runs the same documented lifecycle on every job, so you always know what happens next, what you need to do, and what we deliver.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/contact/">Book Your Free Site Visit</a><a class="button ghost-light" href="/service-area/">View Service Areas</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading reveal"><p class="eyebrow">From First Call to Final Closeout</p><h2>Every job follows the same sequence</h2><p>These stages are not suggestions. They are the operating system used on every project regardless of size.</p></div><div class="lifecycle-stack"><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">1</div><div><span>Project Stage</span><h3>Inquiry and Intake</h3><p>Every project starts with a conversation. You tell us what you need, we confirm the service area, and schedule a site visit.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">2</div><div><span>Project Stage</span><h3>Site Visit</h3><p>We walk the space, measure, photograph existing conditions, and identify issues that cannot be understood from a phone call.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">3</div><div><span>Project Stage</span><h3>Scope Development</h3><p>We define the work, materials, licensed trades, exclusions, and timeline in writing.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">4</div><div><span>Project Stage</span><h3>Estimate Delivery</h3><p>You receive category-based pricing without hidden fees or vague allowances.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">5</div><div><span>Project Stage</span><h3>Contract Signing</h3><p>The agreement references the written scope, price, timeline, and payment schedule.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">6</div><div><span>Project Stage</span><h3>Material Selection</h3><p>Tile, fixtures, counters, flooring, and long-lead materials are locked before demolition.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">7</div><div><span>Project Stage</span><h3>Permit Coordination</h3><p>When permits are required, we handle applications, scheduling, and municipal follow-up.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">8</div><div><span>Project Stage</span><h3>Demolition</h3><p>Existing materials come out per scope. Hidden conditions are documented before the plan changes.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">9</div><div><span>Licensed Trades</span><h3>Rough-In</h3><p>Licensed plumbers, electricians, and HVAC professionals install behind-the-wall systems, with photos before closure.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">10</div><div><span>Licensed Trades</span><h3>Inspection</h3><p>Municipal inspections verify code compliance before walls close. We coordinate and attend.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">11</div><div><span>Quality Gate</span><h3>Signature Finish Protocol</h3><p>Our internal quality gate reviews every finished element against the written scope and photo record.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">12</div><div><span>Project Stage</span><h3>Final Walkthrough</h3><p>You review the completed project point by point. Anything remaining is documented.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">13</div><div><span>Project Stage</span><h3>Punch List Resolution</h3><p>Every punch item is addressed before closeout and final sign-off.</p></div></article><article class="lifecycle-card reveal"><div class="stage-number">14</div><div><span>Project Stage</span><h3>Completion and Closeout</h3><p>You receive warranty details, care notes, final documentation, and a closed project file.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section dark"><div class="shell split"><div class="reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Why This Process Matters</p><h2>Documentation removes the guesswork that causes renovation problems.</h2><p>Running every project through a documented lifecycle takes more effort. It also means you know where the project stands, you have a written record, and decisions do not disappear into verbal conversations.</p></div><div class="principle-grid reveal"><div><b>Written</b><span>Scopes and approvals</span></div><div><b>Visible</b><span>Photo-verified stages</span></div><div><b>Accountable</b><span>Named owners at every step</span></div><div><b>Closed</b><span>No loose ends at handoff</span></div></div></div></section>
